 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Of course. Often, simple gestures mean a lot. He might enjoy a favorite food, a warm glass of milk before bed, or being helped with simple tasks. Then, a simple yes no system can help. Ask him to say yes if he wants it. He' soon find out words he never knew he forgot. A large mirror, a bright room, or seeing a doctor about sight checking are good. Having a schedule can help him too. Start with simple map and stick to it. Try to take it step by step. He' doing well to ask for help, so encourage that. He might surprise you.",
